{"schema_version": "1.0", "session_id": "42b9fb43-99d0-48a1-bb9b-f0ae0d506614", "team_id": "contest2026_223_hepingdechengshi", "github_login": "lthxxn", "tool": "claude-code", "seq": 235, "ts": "2026-09-19T16:34:29.794Z", "role": "tool", "tool_name": "<result>", "tool_call_id": "tooluse_JJDZKcdIxAj9D2FaFBH2gl", "input": null, "output": "60\t\n61\t  /* SVCALL is system handler 11 */\n62\t\n63\t  regval  = getreg32(NVIC_SYSH8_11_PRIORITY);\n64\t  regval &= ~NVIC_SYSH_PRIORITY_PR11_MASK;\n65\t  regval |= (priority << NVIC_SYSH_PRIORITY_PR11_SHIFT);\n66\t  putreg32(regval, NVIC_SYSH8_11_PRIORITY);\n67\t}\n68\tvoid arm_ack_irq(int irq) {}\n69\tvoid common_irq_initialize_on_core(void) {\n70\t    uint32_t regaddr;\n71\t  int num_priority_registers;\n72\t  /* Make sure the NVIC uses the NuttX vector table.  The per-CPU reset\n73\t   * handlers already point SCB->VTOR at _vectors, but assert it here too so\n74\t   * SVC (and the other exceptions) dispatch through exception_common.\n75\t   */\n76\t  putreg32((uint32_t)_vectors, NVIC_VECTAB);\n77\t\n78\t  /* Attach the SVCall and Hard Fault exception handlers.  SVCall is the\n79\t   * context-switch mechanism (sys_call0 -> svc #0); HardFault must also be\n80\t   * caught because an SVCall can escalate to HardFault when raised from\n81\t   * within an ISR of equal or higher priority.\n82\t   */\n83\t  irq_attach(NVIC_IRQ_SVCALL, arm_svcall, NULL);\n84\t  irq_attach(NVIC_IRQ_HARDFAULT, arm_hardfault, NULL);\n85\t\n86\t  /* Attach the other configurable fault handlers.  Without these a\n87\t   * MemManage/BusFault/UsageFault would land in the Default_Handler\n88\t   * infinite loop (no call stack to inspect), which is what the SHCSR\n89\t   * MEMFAULTENA bit enables.  arm_memfault/arm_busfault/arm_usagefault\n90\t   * are declared in arm_internal.h and compiled into libarch.\n91\t   */\n92\t  irq_attach(NVIC_IRQ_MEMFAULT, arm_memfault, NULL);\n93\t  irq_attach(NVIC_IRQ_BUSFAULT, arm_busfault, NULL);\n94\t  irq_attach(NVIC_IRQ_USAGEFAULT, arm_usagefault, NULL);\n95\t\n96\t  /* The Beken boot path leaves both masks raised with raw CMSIS ops (NOT the\n97\t   * NuttX up_irq_disable(), which only raises BASEPRI): __start() does\n98\t   * `cpsid i` (PRIMASK=1), and soc_isr_init()/arch_isr_entry_init() ->\n99\t   * arch_int_init_all_irq() does `cpsid f` (FAULTMASK=1) + `cpsid i`.  If we\n100\t   * leave them set, the first context switch (SVC via sys_call0, and\n101\t   * PendSV/SysTick too) is masked and never taken: no exception ever reaches\n102\t   * arm_doirq and the scheduler hangs in thread mode.  Undo them the same\n103\t   * way: `cpsie f` clears FAULTMASK, `cpsie i` clears PRIMASK.\n104\t   */\n105\t  putreg32(DEFPRIORITY32, NVIC_SYSH4_7_PRIORITY);\n106\t  putreg32(DEFPRIORITY32, NVIC_SYSH8_11_PRIORITY);\n107\t  putreg32(DEFPRIORITY32, NVIC_SYSH12_15_PRIORITY);\n108\t  beken_prioritize_syscall(NVIC_SYSH_SVCALL_PRIORITY);\n109\t\n110\t  num_priority_registers = (getreg32(NVIC_ICTR) + 1) * 8;\n111\t\n112\t  /* Now set all of the interrupt lines to the default priority */\n113\t\n114\t  regaddr = NVIC_IRQ0_3_PRIORITY;\n115\t  while (num_priority_registers--)\n116\t    {\n117\t      putreg32(DEFPRIORITY32, regaddr);\n118\t      regaddr += 4;\n119\t    }", "is_error": false}
